                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "da735a37-191f-34f2-8837-5504114d26fa",
                        "entry_id": "81e8192f-2592-3ad3-b9a3-a08c483465cb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Impossible to be searched; inscrutable; impenetrable."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c18b4f14-05c4-4dc1-9b5b-58545d07d304",
                                "sense_id": "da735a37-191f-34f2-8837-5504114d26fa",
                                "text": "By the presaging of the seven planets, And by the searchless sources of the Nile, And by the prayers of Christian and of Heathen , And by the elements earth, air and fire, That hold within their intermingled veins The secret of illimitable life—By fate and time and God—I here conjure you"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2a1a9add-11df-41b0-80d9-fbc51a2624f7",
                                "sense_id": "da735a37-191f-34f2-8837-5504114d26fa",
                                "text": "Th'inticing Smile; the modest-seeming eye, Beneath whose Beaueous Beams, belying Heaven, Lurk searchless Cunning, Cruelty, and Death: And still, false-warbling in his cheated Ear, Her syren Voice, enchanting, draws him on, To guileful Shores, and Meads of fatal Joy."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4c7ce64a-d5e3-4557-9f72-f8a34a7a96e6",
                                "sense_id": "da735a37-191f-34f2-8837-5504114d26fa",
                                "text": "Famine, murder, hell and power Were glutted in that glorious hour Which searchless fate had stamped for me With the seal of her security"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "14ec9d9c-0f98-4c78-b62f-c2648682e236",
                                "sense_id": "da735a37-191f-34f2-8837-5504114d26fa",
                                "text": "Though others faint—though erring nature stray, Guard thou the searchless mandate,—and Obey!"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "80778bae-2e03-3c9e-9ef8-61c31033a405",
                        "entry_id": "81e8192f-2592-3ad3-b9a3-a08c483465cb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Vast; Too massive or great to be fully known."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "dd8e8fef-9b4b-490b-bff1-e62a4a0381ca",
                                "sense_id": "80778bae-2e03-3c9e-9ef8-61c31033a405",
                                "text": "O Goodness searchless! Thou who once didst walk With man on earth, with man familiar talk,!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9759f774-8195-44a0-9f1e-d9a13feb3147",
                                "sense_id": "80778bae-2e03-3c9e-9ef8-61c31033a405",
                                "text": "I'll sing the searchless depths of the compassion divine, The depths unfathomed yet By reason's plummet and the line of wit, - Too light the plummet and too short the line;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7df77f27-3f31-4699-a76b-a09d66cabf29",
                                "sense_id": "80778bae-2e03-3c9e-9ef8-61c31033a405",
                                "text": "Facing the East, and its searchless savannas— Facing the gloom of the thicket and forest;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2966df87-6caf-43b3-ace5-2081d3007cee",
                                "sense_id": "80778bae-2e03-3c9e-9ef8-61c31033a405",
                                "text": "It is better to remember Mr. Boyd gratefully as the author of the beautiful communion hymn, \"O teach us, Lord, Thy searchless love to know,\" than as one who inadvertently perpetrated a doctrinal deviation which contributed to a minor ecclesiastical cleavage."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c9b16d07-b092-3544-a26f-345970ca0b70",
                        "entry_id": "81e8192f-2592-3ad3-b9a3-a08c483465cb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "That arrives at a solution by analytic means, rather than by trial and error or iterative searching."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ddec50d8-af4b-4b88-a850-a69e642d9267",
                                "sense_id": "c9b16d07-b092-3544-a26f-345970ca0b70",
                                "text": "Finding of the optimum regime, corresponding to the extremum of the quality index, may be carried out by an automatic search (search and extremal ACS) or by a searchless way ( searchless or analytical ACS)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7a8bfd1f-f5b1-4a4a-b5f4-a73a48e28953",
                                "sense_id": "c9b16d07-b092-3544-a26f-345970ca0b70",
                                "text": "As an alternative and an extension to the trial-and-error adaptation employed in systems with extremum-seeking regulatory mechanisms is the idea of direct, searchless optimization proposed in the 1960s."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5423e101-c713-4329-a185-6e6294fe0ccb",
                                "sense_id": "c9b16d07-b092-3544-a26f-345970ca0b70",
                                "text": "The control is sought in the class of searchless self-adjustable systems that provide the linearity of the basic adjusting contour if the object state deviates from the unperturbed movement."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "44620b38-67c3-4249-9a9c-475f55f3297e",
                                "sense_id": "c9b16d07-b092-3544-a26f-345970ca0b70",
                                "text": "Similarly, in [99], a discrete wavelet transform is used alongside the parallel implementation of FIC. Jackson et al. [88] exercised a searchless approach to encode the image using FIC and claimed to achieve a higher compression ratio."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
